  "implementation": [
    "Only already-admitted stateless Binding/Native __kvGet requests can select the private query route. Original namespace authorization and fresh discovery/enrollment/FIFO selection remain; newly enrolled cells use the original schema command.",
    "The query runs before choosing a mutation sequence and shares existing KV entry/graph codecs. It reads initialized inline values or misses from one immutable selected image. Value/tag/metadata lengths are inspected before loading variable returned buffers; result vectors grow within conservative codec headroom, and the final native frame is bounded exactly.",
    "A private structured-null eligibility result selects the original command for missing schema, external values, JSON response shaping or oversized results. Input, nonce, original deadline, logical request count and admission remain fixed. Arbitrary read errors never select a command fallback.",
    "The private query contract rejects stale consistency before decoding. S3-minimum namespaces require the selected image archive proof through the existing query verifier; no archive/body/pin/source-journal proof is removed. Stateful source calls and external-value protocol remain unchanged.",
    "No worker, byte/item bank, protocol marker, VM/resource, original RustFS fixture or durability-proof limit change."
  ],
